# Lightsail deployment rule

This repository deploys to a Lightsail server at `/home/admin/portfolio`.

## Core policy

- GitHub is the single source of truth for production code.
- Make code changes locally in Cursor, commit locally, and push to GitHub.
- Do not create or edit tracked source files directly on the Lightsail server unless the user explicitly asks for emergency hotfix work.
- Do not leave behind backup copies, rescue files, or alternate versions of tracked files on the server.
- Do not use ad hoc deploy flows that stash tracked files on the server, copy random folders into production, or modify tracked files outside Git.

## Production process manager

- Production is managed by PM2.
- The PM2 app name is `portfolio-gate`.
- Do not use `nohup node ...` for this app.
- Do not manually start a second Node process for this app.
- When restarting production, use PM2 only.

## Required deploy sequence

When the user asks to deploy, publish, push and deploy, or update production, use this sequence:

1. Check local Git state.
2. Commit only the intended tracked changes.
3. Push to `origin master`.
4. On the Lightsail server, run exactly these commands in `/home/admin/portfolio`:
   - `git pull origin master`
   - `GATE_PASSWORD="$(cat /home/admin/portfolio/.gate-secret)" npm run build`
   - `sudo pm2 restart portfolio-gate --update-env`

## Server safety rules

- Never run `git stash` on the server unless the user explicitly asks for it.
- Never create files like `*.backup`, `*.before-*`, `*.live.*`, or similar rescue copies on the server.
- Never move production files around to work around Git conflicts.
- If `git pull` fails because the server working tree is dirty, stop and report the exact blocking files instead of improvising.
- The server may contain `.gate-secret`, which is required at build/restart time and must never be committed to Git.
- `portfolio-garden.log` is a server-local runtime log and should never be committed.

## Local safety rules

- Untracked local helper files such as `server/production.live.mjs` or `server/production.mjs.before-gate-fix` must not be added unless the user explicitly asks.
- Before committing, verify that only intended tracked files are staged.
- If only untracked local debris exists, explain that it will not be pushed unless explicitly added.

## How to report back

When deployment work is done, report:
- what was committed
- the commit hash
- whether the push succeeded
- whether the server pull succeeded
- whether the build succeeded
- whether the PM2 restart succeeded
- whether any server-local untracked files or dirty-state blockers were detected

## If uncertain

If the server state is not clean or the deployment path is ambiguous, ask before taking destructive action.
